  "hindi": "हे वसुओ, तुम्हारा रक्षक कौन है? तुम्हारा आश्रय देने वाला कौन है? हे द्यावाभूमि, हे अदिति, हमारी रक्षा करो, अधिक बलवान् मनुष्य से, हे वरुण, हे मित्र। हे देवो, यज्ञ में तुम्हारे लिए विस्तृत स्थान कौन देता है?",
  "english": "Who is your protector, O Vasus? Who is your shelterer? O Heaven and Earth, O Aditi, protect us from the mightier mortal, O Varuṇa, O Mitra. Who, O gods, grants wide room for you in the rite?",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "trāsīthām: aorist-type middle 2 du. of √trā; the exact mood is uncertain, rendered as an imperative ('protect'). vaḥ in 'ko vaḥ trātā' taken as genitive 'your'; in 'vaḥ ... varivaḥ dhāti' taken as 'for you'. varivaḥ dhā 'grant wide room' kept literal. sahīyasaḥ martāt: 'from the mightier mortal'; no further identification.",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
