  "hindi": "जिन्होंने पुरातन धामों की स्तुति की, जब वे प्रकाशित हुए — वे असम्मूढ़ पृथक् करने वाले; वे विधाता, निरन्तर रहने वाले, उन्होंने व्यवस्था की; ऋत में चित्त वाले अद्भुत जन चमके।",
  "english": "Those who have praised the ancient abodes, when they shone forth, the unbewildered separators, those arrangers, the unceasing ones, have set in order; the wondrous ones, whose thoughts are on order, have shone.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Difficult verse. Subject of ucchān is not stated (the form is read as 3 pl. of vi-√vas 'shone forth'). viyotāraḥ (vi-√yu) taken as 'separators'; no object of vi dadhuḥ is stated, so none is supplied. arcān is printed with long ā; taken as 3 pl. past of √arc. Whether the several groups of nominatives are the same beings is unclear.",
