  "hindi": "मैं स्तोत्रों से आवास, अदिति, नदी, कल्याण और देवी का मित्रता के लिए आह्वान करता हूँ। जिससे दोनों दिन हमारी रक्षा करें; उषा और रात्रि, ये दोनों अहिंसित, कार्य करें।",
  "english": "With hymns I invoke the dwelling, Aditi, the river, well-being and the goddess, for friendship. So that both days may protect us, let Dawn and Night, the unharmed two, act.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Uncertain. pastyā3m (pluta mark): pastyā 'dwelling' is taken as an accusative object of īḻe; it could instead be an adjective with aditim ('Aditi of the dwelling'). It is unclear which noun devīm qualifies (taken as a further object). 'Sindhu' rendered 'the river'. nipātaḥ = ni pātaḥ read from 'nipāta' before u- (-aḥ + u). karatām has no stated object, none supplied.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
